2028—is developing awareness-raising and training materials to prepare SoHO professionals and entities for the new regulatory framework.\\nASCERTAIN\\nEHA is a partner in the ASCERTAIN project. \", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s171\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 3795, \"end\": 4192, \"text\": \"Hemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nHome\\nAbout EHA\\nEuropean affairs\\nEU-funded projects\\nLeft Sidebar\\n4 min read · May 1, 2025\\nMay 1, 2025\\nShare\\nEuropean affairs\\nPolicy and advocacy\\nRegulatory affairs and scientific relations\\nStakeholder involvement and alliances\\nEU-funded projects\\nEU funding calls\\nEU-funded projects\\nOur ongoing projects\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s173\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 4529, \"end\": 4900, \"text\": \"ASCERTAIN stands for Affordability and Sustainability improvements through new pricing, Cost- Effectiveness and ReimbursemenT models to Appraise INnovative health technologies.\\nThe project is the result of years of advocacy and multistakeholder discussions, and is funded by the EU’s Horizon Europe program.​ It seeks to promote:\\nAccess to affordable health technologies\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s174\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 4900, \"end\": 5266, \"text\": \"The need to stimulate innovation and entrepreneurship\\nThe need to consider the environmental impact of innovations\\nASCERTAIN will develop open-access, easy to use, policy-supporting tools including pricing, cost-effectiveness, and reimbursement models. These should:\\nImprove transparency and accountability of decision-making\\nReduce uncertainty for all stakeholders\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s175\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 5266, \"end\": 5651, \"text\": \"Reward innovation in areas of high unmet need\\nAccelerate access for patients\\nSupport long-term planning in a sustainable way\\nIn ASCERTAIN, EHA collaborates with academic institutions, public health organizations, professional associations, patient organizations, and healthcare and technology companies from across Europe.\\nThe project ends in November 2026.\\nLearn more about ASCERTAIN\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s176\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 5651, \"end\": 5931, \"text\": \"Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Projects\\nThe Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions fund excellent research and innovation and equip researchers at all stages of their career with new knowledge and skills, through mobility across borders and exposure to different sectors and disciplines. \", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s177\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 5931, \"end\": 6061, \"text\": \"The MSCA help build Europe’s capacity for research and innovation by investing in the long-term careers of excellent researchers.\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s178\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 6061, \"end\": 6456, \"text\": \"To foster doctoral and postdoctoral basic/translational research in hematology, EHA is partnering with MSCA networks operating in hematology, offering dissemination of calls and research outcomes, networking opportunities for trainees, and expertise for education and trainings developed by the networks.\\nEHA is a current associated partner of:\\nMSCA-DN TOLERATE\\nMSCA-DN FANTOM\\nMSCA-DN InnoCAR-T\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s179\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 6456, \"end\": 6704, \"text\": \"MSCA-DN MIRACLE\\nMSCA-DN ACHILLES\\nMSCA-COFUND CArrerasPathfinders\\nPrevious projects\\nSUPPLY\\nDue to the importance of plasma for hematology, EHA joined the SUPPLY (Strengthening voluntary non-remunerated plasma collection capacity in Europe) project.\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s180\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 6704, \"end\": 7098, \"text\": \"This consortium, which received funding from the EU4Health program and was coordinated by the European Blood Alliance, was made up of 20 diverse stakeholders. From September 2022 to February 2024, they worked together to evaluate legal frameworks and policies on plasma collection in Europe.\\nEHA led the SUPPLY work package on:\\nDeveloping recommendations on the clinical use of immunoglobulins\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s181\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 7098, \"end\": 7460, \"text\": \"The prioritization of such use in times of crisis\\nThe final recommendations, with input from EHA experts Cynthia So-Osman (transfusion medicine) and Isabelle Durand-Zaleski (public health and health economics), can be found in the report on SUPPLY work package 6.\\nAll the reports resulting from the project are available on the SUPPLY resources webpage.\\nHARMONY\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s182\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 7460, \"end\": 7837, \"text\": \"EHA was a partner in the HARMONY and HARMONY PLUS projects, funded by the Innovative Medicines Initiative (IMI, now IHI), from 2017 through 2024.\\nHARMONY leveraged big data to help improve the care of patients with blood cancers. It gathered, integrated and analyzed anonymous patient data to define clinical endpoints and outcomes that are recognized by all key stakeholders.\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s183\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 7837, \"end\": 8103, \"text\": \"The project’s data sharing platform aimed to facilitate research as well as decision making by both policy makers and clinicians.\\nGAPP Joint Action\\nWe were a collaborating stakeholder in the GAPP Joint Action, which ran from 2018 to 2021.\\nGAPP main objectives were:\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s184\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 8103, \"end\": 8493, \"text\": \"Increasing consistency and efficacy of competent authority regulatory activities through harmonization of EU-level tools for authorization procedures for preparation processes at blood and tissues establishments\\nDeveloping a concept model for a European knowledge-sharing platform to support competent authorities in the assessment and evaluation of novel preparation processes of products\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s185\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 8493, \"end\": 8885, \"text\": \"Developing an international network of (trained) experts to support competent authorities in these tasks\\nEUnetHTA and EUnetHTA 21\\nEHA supported the work of the EUnetHTA consortium. This project piloted collaboration between EU Member States on Health Technology Assessment (HTA), by identifying and facilitating the involvement of leading experts in hematology in joint clinical assessments.\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s186\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 8885, \"end\": 9279, \"text\": \"Our support to EUnetHTA is an example of how we ensure that the expert views of hematologists are considered in all relevant EU decision-making and regulatory processes.\\nEHA also provided input to the EUnetHTA 21 consortium which was commissioned with developing methodologies, guidance and a stakeholder framework for the implementation of the HTAR.\\nShare\\nEuropean affairs\\nPolicy and advocacy\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s187\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 9279, \"end\": 9658, \"text\": \"Regulatory affairs and scientific relations\\nStakeholder involvement and alliances\\nEU-funded projects\\nEU funding calls\\nJoin EHA\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\n60-day trial\\nGet involved\\nCareer development\\nScientific meetings\\nAbout us\\nMission and vision\\nJobs\\nSponsor EHA\\nContact us\\nFollow us\\nPrivacy statement\\nTerms and conditions\\nSubscribe\\nCopyright © 2026\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s161\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 399, \"text\": \"EU-funded projects - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EU-funded projects - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\\nEU-funded projects - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\\nEU-funded projects - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nConnect & Network\\nClinical practice\\nEducation & Training\\nResearch & Innovation\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA2027 Congress\\n\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"time_metadata\": {}}, {\"id\": \"s162\", \"doc_id\": \"web-6ccbe1697a1d87cfbf01eca9\", \"start\": 399, \"end\": 785, \"text\": \"Congress archive\\nScientific meetings\\nMembership\\nEHA2027 registr